  "name": "Add burned-in captions to any video (12 styles, karaoke fill, natural line breaks)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "896dd517-d7f2-58a8-a25c-e986d10f08c1",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -820,
        -280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 600,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## \ud83c\udfac Add burned-in captions to any video\n\n![Karaoke fill captions on a streamer video](https://caption.yosuga.dev/samples/video/demo2-karaoke_fill.gif)\n\nPaste a video URL into a form and get the video back **with captions burned in**: transcribed, split at natural phrase breaks and styled with one of **12 caption styles**, such as karaoke fill and word pop.\n\n### How it works\n1. The form collects a video URL, a caption style, a language and optional keywords\n2. The [Video Subtitle & Transcript API](https://rapidapi.com/yosuga-yosuga-default/api/video-subtitle-transcript-api1) transcribes the audio with word timestamps, breaks lines where a reader expects them and burns the captions in\n3. The workflow checks the job every 15 seconds\n4. The form page shows download links for the MP4 and the SRT\n\n### Setup\n1. Subscribe to the API on RapidAPI (the free BASIC plan includes 30 min/month)\n2. Create a **Header Auth** credential: name `X-RapidAPI-Key`, value your RapidAPI key\n3. Select it in **Create captioning job** and **Get job**\n4. Click **Test workflow** and submit the form. Leave the URL empty to try the 8-second demo clip\n\n### Customization\n- Compare the 12 styles in the [style gallery](https://yosuga.dev/n8n/caption-styles-demo.jpg) or tune one in [Caption Studio](https://yosuga.dev/app/caption/), then paste its `caption_style` into **Create captioning job**\n- **Keywords** (names, product terms) improve recognition, and the `keyword_color` style colors them\n- Burn-in languages: English, Japanese, Spanish, Portuguese, French, German, Turkish, Indonesian, Hindi\n- Billed per minute only when the job succeeds. BASIC adds a small watermark\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a909800b-6be9-5618-96b6-7cb2cb63a8e2",
